<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saint Vitus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 303</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saint Vitus was an early Christian martyr from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>, said to have died in the persecution under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diocletian">Diocletian</a>. His relics were brought from Saint-Denis to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> abbey of Corvey in 836, spreading his cult across central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, and he is the patron of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a>'s cathedral. The name St Vitus' Dance, for chorea, comes from the dancing once held before his images.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saint-vitus.jpg" alt="Saint Vitus" width="320" height="317" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: BSonne · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:St_Veit_G%C3%B6lsen_Pfarrkirche_Fenster02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
